Upstream PR #387 (merged 2026-10-21; Toro Lets Party's patch 3009, carried as is): the PPU lifter finds a jump table's bounds compare
beyond the 30-instruction window, in the function-bounded live window, before the 256-entry fallback. Toro's text:
PPU lifter: find a jump table's bounds compare beyond the 30-instruction window. General fix (upstream candidate,
needs the PM's OK). When no `cmp[l]wi rIdx, N` sits in the 30 instructions before the `bctr`, the scan fell back
to 256 entries; a larger table was cut there. Toro Lets Party func_000A2EC8's script-opcode dispatcher (bctr 0xA2FE0,
table 0xA2FE4, 292 entries, `cmplwi r29,0x123` at 0xA2F5C = 33 instructions before) lost 27 of its 208 targets
(indices 258+): index 263 = 0xA3B10 became `[ppu] unresolved indirect call` and the logo scene setup ran on garbage
(the RE notes s.9). Now the function-bounded live window (win_cand, already used for the table base) is searched
for the compare before the 256 fallback; the structural and first-hole stops still end the scan. JT_DEBUG prints the
count found there. Check: JT_DEBUG=0xA2FE0 -> count 291, 208 targets.
diff --git a/tools/ppu_lifter.py b/tools/ppu_lifter.py
index 927fdcc..fc7b619 100644
--- a/tools/ppu_lifter.py
+++ b/tools/ppu_lifter.py
@@ -4657,6 +4657,26 @@ def discover_jump_tables(all_insns, read_u32, toc, text_lo, text_hi, func_starts
                             continue
                         if count is None or _c > count:
                             count = _c
+            # No compare in the 30-insn window: look through the function-bounded
+            # live window (win_cand) for it. The bounds check can sit further from
+            # the bctr than 30 insns (Toro Lets Party func_000A2EC8: `cmplwi r29,
+            # 0x123` at 0xA2F5C is 33 insns before the bctr at 0xA2FE0), and the
+            # 256 fallback then cut its 292-entry table: 27 opcode handlers
+            # (indices 258+) fell through to an unresolved indirect call
+            # (0xA3B10, index 263) and the script interpreter ran on garbage.
+            if count is None:
+                for w in reversed(win_cand):
+                    if w.mnemonic in ('cmplwi', 'cmpwi'):
+                        a = [x.strip() for x in w.operands.split(',')]
+                        _cmp_reg = a[1] if (a and a[0].startswith('cr')) else (a[0] if a else None)
+                        if _cmp_reg == _raw_idx:
+                            try:
+                                _c = int(a[-1], 0)
+                            except ValueError:
+                                continue
+                            if count is None or _c > count:
+                                count = _c
+                _dbg(all_insns[i].addr, f"count from the live window: {count}")
             if count is None or count < 0 or count > 4096:
                 count = 256
